    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes owner responses include a computed `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName`. The test creates an owner and reads back `displayName` via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, and both create and read responses share the same `OwnerMapper`, so the fix lives in the DTO schema + mapper rather than any single endpoint pipeline.\n\nTwo edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` property (readOnly string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` computing `displayName` as `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()` from the stored names.\n\nSince the field is `readOnly`, it never binds from request bodies and only appears in responses, matching the spec's \"from the stored names.\"",
